.\" The feeder's man page, for the site's man-pager clip (site/tapes/man.tape).
.TH FEEDER 1 2026-10-02 "feeder 0.3" "Cat Feeder Manual"
.SH NAME
feeder \- dispense a cat's meals on schedule
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B feeder
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR grams ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR count ]
.RB [ run | now | status ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B feeder
reads the day's meals from the SD card and turns the auger at each one until
the portion is out, 2.5 g a turn.
A turn that takes longer than 650 ms counts as a jam: the auger backs up half a
turn and tries again.
.PP
Every turn, jam and meal is written to the log, which
.BR ada (1)
reads well.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config =\fIfile\fR
Read the schedule from
.I file
instead of
.IR /sd/feeder.toml .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Count the turns and log them, and keep the kibble.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-portion =\fIgrams\fR
Dispense
.I grams
at every meal, whatever the schedule says.
Ada would like this to be larger.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-retries =\fIcount\fR
Retry a jammed turn up to
.I count
times before giving up (default 3).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Wait for the next meal, dispense it, and repeat.
The default.
.TP
.B now
Dispense one portion at once.
Neumann has learned the sound of this command.
.TP
.B status
Print the next meal, the grams left in the hopper, and the last jam.
.SH SCHEDULE
.SS Meals
Each
.B [[meal]]
has a time and a portion in grams:
07:00 20 g, 12:00 15 g, 22:00 10 g.
.SS By hand
A meal with no portion is served by hand; the feeder only logs that it was due.
Dinner at 17:00 is one, at Ada's insistence.
.SS Skipped days
A
.B skip
list of dates leaves those days out, for the vet's fasting rules.
Ada has not been told about this.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FEEDER_LOG
Where the log goes, in place of
.IR /sd/log.txt .
.TP
.B TZ
The time zone the schedule is in.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sd/feeder.toml
The schedule.
.TP
.I /sd/log.txt
One line a turn, a jam, or a paw on the lid.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the feeder was stopped, 1 when a turn stayed jammed after every retry,
and 2 when the hopper ran empty.
.SH BUGS
A paw on the lid stops the motor mid-turn.
Ada has learned this, and that a stopped motor is followed by a human.
.PP
Who opened the cheese drawer is still unsolved.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ada (1),
.BR crontab (5),
.BR neumann (7)
